# EVERY FILE CHECKS OUT WITH LF, ON EVERY MACHINE.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is true on this machine, so a checkout rewrote app.js,
# index.html and styles.css with CRLF line endings. The checks match on `\n`,
# so a two-line pattern stopped matching and five of them failed on code that
# had not changed. Measured 22 September 2026: the swipe checks went from 108
# of 108 to 103, and two other guards crashed on a slice that came back empty.
#
# NOTHING WAS WRONG WITH THE CODE. A clone on a Windows machine would have
# seen the same, so this was never only a local accident.
#
# THE REPO IS TEXT AND IT IS LF. That is what the files hold, it is what the
# checks read, and it is what the browser is served.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never touches the bytes.
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.apk binary
*.aab binary
*.keystore binary
*.jar binary
